From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haybarn <noreply@query.farm>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Raise the header line limit to 16 KiB

GitHub release-asset redirects send a single content-security-policy
line of 9,243 bytes (since 2026-10-24), over the 8 KiB default, and the
response is then rejected as a read error.

diff --git a/third_party/httplib/httplib.hpp b/third_party/httplib/httplib.hpp
index 5675d76..29747d0 100644
--- a/third_party/httplib/httplib.hpp
+++ b/third_party/httplib/httplib.hpp
@@ -116,7 +116,9 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifndef CPPHTTPLIB_HEADER_MAX_LENGTH
-#define CPPHTTPLIB_HEADER_MAX_LENGTH 8192
+// One header line, name and value. GitHub's release-asset redirects send a
+// content-security-policy line of more than 9 KiB, so 8 KiB is too small.
+#define CPPHTTPLIB_HEADER_MAX_LENGTH 16384
 #endif
 
 #ifndef CPPHTTPLIB_HEADER_MAX_COUNT
-- 
2.43.0

